description:
FILED s517a (Opus, 2026-10-15) -- the producers #3242 did NOT route through p-bool.

#3242 (stable booleans) made p-bool return the interned +p-yes+ / +p-no+ and
routed: ! / not, the 12 comparisons, defined, exists (hash / array / sub),
isa, xor, !~, builtin::true / false / is_bool / is_weak, re::is_regexp,
Internals::SvREADONLY, scalar stat, created_as_* (excludes booleans).

perl 5.40.3 ALSO returns a boolean (is_bool true; probed scratch/s517a/pr/b1.pl)
from these, which PCL still answers with a plain 1 / "" (is_bool false):
  - filetests whose stat SUCCEEDED: -e -f -d -r -z ... (false = "" BOOL; a
    failed stat is undef, not a boolean -- matches PCL already, #403);
    -s is a SIZE (not a boolean);
  - eof($fh)   (PCL answers undef at "not eof" -- a second difference);
  - m// in scalar context, true and false;
  - s/// that does NOT match ("" BOOL; a match returns the count, not bool);
  - utf8::is_utf8 / utf8::valid;
  - wantarray (true and false);
  - defined &name (p-sub-defined: true is (make-p-box 1), FALSE is undef where
    perl gives "" -- a second difference).
Each is one p-bool call at its return; probe each with is_bool vs perl and
add rows to Pl/t/stable-bool-01.t's producer row.
